import Gimle.Forseti.PolynomialTrapping
import Gimle.Forseti.Examples.GalerkinNS.T3Below12

-- the closed forms below have hundreds of rational terms; elaborating them needs room
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

/-! # The 3-mode member below `E ≤ 9`: a degree-4 tube around its focus

`T3Below12` traps an ellipsoid inside `E ≤ 12`. This module traps a sublevel set
`V ≤ 1` of a **degree-4** polynomial, a thin tube around the stable focus the
start approaches in simulation (not a Lean statement), found by the same search
with the whole orbit held inside (gimle-forseti's task 214): on it
`V' ≤ α (inner − V)` holds with `inner < 1` by an explicit sum of squares with an
S-procedure multiplier, and the set lies in `{E ≤ 9}` by an S-lemma certificate,
so the energy observation stays in `[0, 9]` for all time: the member's standing
undecided claim was `E ≤ 10`. The certificate is in the Cholesky form of
`K5Below6`; all numbers are rational and every identity is `ring`. -/

namespace Gimle.Forseti.Examples.GalerkinNS.T3

open Gimle.Asgard Gimle.Asgard.Dynamics Gimle.Asgard.Polynomial Gimle.Forseti Gimle.Forseti.Trajectory

